  "changes": [
    "Added an inherited bounded socket with session, executable, registry, policy and resource-assignment binding.",
    "Bound each existing single-use launch token to the persistent session and exact typed request.",
    "Retained the workspace through idle intervals, GPU drain/teardown, shutdown accounting and observed successful child exit.",
    "Kept journal reservations on handshake, transport, decoding and process-exit failures for explicit recovery.",
    "Added the explicit typed-process-dag backend to single-GPU and fleet controllers and the benchmark report.",
    "Retained immutable worker-session bytes and distinct child-start/exit records."
  ],
  "delivered_transactions_measured": false,
  "fresh_work": {
    "complete_gpu_roots": 1,
    "native_blocks_applied": 0,
    "recursive_proofs": 8,
    "wallet_proofs": 0
  },
  "git_commit": "094cade18a59d38d7d65bd805511a7809b348a9e",
  "known_limits": [
    "Only one eight-input root on the RTX 5080 Laptop GPU is qualified for this binary/backend. The desktop GPU, concurrent children and larger counts remain unqualified for it.",
    "This run used the full single-worker allocation: 23 Rayon threads, 44.75 GiB worker RAM, 7 GiB managed VRAM and 7.25 GiB conservative context allowance.",
    "The benchmark monitor interruption leaves a host telemetry gap. Worker-owned timing, GPU context logs and ExecStopPost cgroup peak/event counters remain retained. This is not a matched speedup claim.",
    "Each bounded service still owns one candidate DAG. Native arrival integration and a shared owner across multiple GPU workers remain open.",
    "No active GPU-worker or DAG-owner restart was qualified. Clean completed-journal recovery remains separately qualified by the earlier inline-worker evidence.",
    "Existing public wallet proofs and keys were reused. Delivered transaction throughput, cold full-64, post-seal timing and production readiness are not established."
  ],
